1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,750
I'm Felix, and together with
my team at Moonshot,

2
00:00:02,810 --> 00:00:05,650
we built Recount on top of Cala.

3
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:08,290
Cala knows who founded
which company,

4
00:00:08,350 --> 00:00:11,880
who led each round
and where founders worked before.

5
00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:14,470
Recount turns all of that into signals

6
00:00:14,530 --> 00:00:17,440
that you can use in order
to make decisions.

7
00:00:17,610 --> 00:00:20,880
Investors use the signals
to find great companies early.

8
00:00:21,010 --> 00:00:23,310
Founders use them
to find the right investors.

9
00:00:23,370 --> 00:00:26,230
Recount has
more than 30 signals.

10
00:00:26,290 --> 00:00:30,090
Did the company raise money
in the 2022 downturn?

11
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:32,550
Did the old investors
put in more money?

12
00:00:32,610 --> 00:00:35,050
Has the founder built
a company before?

13
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:38,540
How long did they stay
at their last job?

14
00:00:38,610 --> 00:00:42,950
Just type what you want,
like a good fintech company.

15
00:00:43,010 --> 00:00:44,910
Recount picks the filter for you.

16
00:00:44,970 --> 00:00:48,170
We tested every signal
in a fair way.

17
00:00:48,230 --> 00:00:50,530
We hid the last few years of data

18
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:52,990
and checked which signals
really worked.

19
00:00:53,050 --> 00:00:56,190
Most tools just give you a score.
We tested ours.

20
00:00:56,250 --> 00:01:00,510
We checked 35 signals on years
of data they had never seen.

21
00:01:00,570 --> 00:01:03,630
Now you know which signal
really works.

22
00:01:03,690 --> 00:01:04,770
Here's an example.

23
00:01:04,830 --> 00:01:08,550
An investor wants founders
who built a company before

24
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:10,720
and come from research.

25
00:01:10,810 --> 00:01:13,250
Recount finds Anton Osika.

26
00:01:13,310 --> 00:01:16,890
He worked at CERN, was the first
engineer at Sana Labs

27
00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:18,870
and founded Depict.

28
00:01:18,930 --> 00:01:21,890
In late 2023,
he started Lovable.

29
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:24,930
Less than a year later,
top investors backed it.

30
00:01:25,170 --> 00:01:28,480
And today, Lovable is worth
over 10 billion dollars.

31
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:30,520
Founders can use it too.

32
00:01:30,630 --> 00:01:32,830
Paste the investor you want to meet.

33
00:01:32,890 --> 00:01:35,410
Recount sorts them
into three groups.

34
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:38,310
Who to pitch first,
who backs a different round size,

35
00:01:38,370 --> 00:01:41,110
and who mostly just follows.

36
00:01:41,170 --> 00:01:45,090
For each fund, you see how often
it led rounds like yours,

37
00:01:45,150 --> 00:01:46,510
who bought the companies it backed,

38
00:01:46,570 --> 00:01:49,720
and who in your network
can introduce you.

39
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:51,430
Recount, powered by Cala.

40
00:01:51,490 --> 00:01:53,350
The right companies for investors,

41
00:01:53,450 --> 00:01:54,600
the right investors for founders.
